{"id":79,"name":"slowpoke","speciesId":79,"dex":79,"form":"normal","generation":1,"types":["water","psychic"],"stats":{"hp":90,"attack":65,"defense":65,"special-attack":40,"special-defense":40,"speed":15},"abilities":[{"name":"oblivious","hidden":false},{"name":"own-tempo","hidden":false},{"name":"regenerator","hidden":true}],"height":12,"weight":360,"baseExp":63,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/79.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/79.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/79.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/79.ogg","genus":"Dopey Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon idiota","flavor":[{"version":"red","text":"Incredibly slow and dopey. It takes 5 seconds for it to feel pain when under attack."},{"version":"yellow","text":"Incredibly slow and sluggish. It is quite content to loll about without worrying about the time."},{"version":"gold","text":"It lazes vacantly near water. If something bites its tail, it won't even notice for a whole day."},{"version":"silver","text":"A sweet sap leaks from its tail's tip. Although not nutritious, the tail is pleasant to chew on."},{"version":"crystal","text":"It is always so absent-minded that it won't react, even if its flavorful tail is bitten."},{"version":"ruby","text":"SLOWPOKE uses its tail to catch prey by dipping it in water at the side of a river. However, this POKéMON often forgets what it’s doing and often spends entire days just loafing at water’s edge."},{"version":"emerald","text":"It catches prey by dipping its tail in water at the side of a river. But it often forgets what it is doing and spends entire days just loafing at water’s edge."},{"version":"firered","text":"It is always vacantly lost in thought, but no one knows what it is thinking about. It is good at fishing with its tail."},{"version":"leafgreen","text":"Incredibly slow and dopey. It takes five seconds for it to feel pain when under attack."},{"version":"diamond","text":"Although slow, it is skilled at fishing with its tail. It does not feel pain if its tail is bitten."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"It lazes vacantly near water. If something bites its tail, it won’t even notice for a whole day."},{"version":"soulsilver","text":"A sweet sap leaks from its tail’s tip. Although not nutritious, the tail is pleasant to chew on."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Slowpoke uses its tail to catch prey by dipping it in water at the side of a river. However, this Pokémon often forgets what it’s doing and often spends entire days just loafing at water’s edge."},{"version":"sun","text":"Its long tail often breaks off. It doesn’t really feel any pain, though, and the tail grows back, so Slowpoke isn’t particularly bothered."},{"version":"moon","text":"Alolan home cooking involves drying Slowpoke tails and then simmering them into a salty stew."},{"version":"ultra-sun","text":"There are some places where Slowpoke is worshiped because of a long-standing belief that whenever Slowpoke yawns, it rains."},{"version":"ultra-moon","text":"Although their tails, which fall off naturally, can easily be found lying around, they’re a precious ingredient for cooking."},{"version":"sword","text":"Slow-witted and oblivious, this Pokémon won’t feel any pain if its tail gets eaten. It won’t notice when its tail grows back, either."},{"version":"shield","text":"When this Pokémon’s tail is soaked in water, sweetness seeps from it. Slowpoke uses this trait to lure in and fish up other Pokémon."}],"flavorPt":"Quando a cauda deste Pokémon fica encharcada em água, a doçura escorre dela. Slowpoke usa essa característica para atrair e pescar outros Pokémon.","genderRate":4,"captureRate":190,"eggGroups":["monster","water1"],"isLegendary":false,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"slowpoke","s